651
00:41:40,620 --> 00:41:47,800
And to follow the metaphor to its end, we have to understand the soil, us, doesn't really spread the seed, right?

652
00:41:47,800 --> 00:41:50,280
The fruitful plant creates and drops seed.

653
00:41:50,280 --> 00:41:52,180
And the wind carries it away.

654
00:41:53,860 --> 00:42:03,300
To other places, we're in distant locations, and to stretch the metaphor, even the evil birds carry the seed off so that God uses for good what they intend for evil when they take the seed away, right?

655
00:42:05,780 --> 00:42:07,260
The gospel grows up in us.

656
00:42:07,260 --> 00:42:13,340
It is a natural matter, of course, begins to just spread and multiply itself into the lives of others around us.

657
00:42:13,340 --> 00:42:16,740
We are not responsible for making the word grow down deep in us.

658
00:42:16,740 --> 00:42:20,760
We are responsible for listening, listening well and responding.

659
00:42:20,760 --> 00:42:25,340
So we want to understand these parables and have the appropriate way to respond to each, okay?

660
00:42:26,220 --> 00:42:30,300
We want to really open, listen fully for things that we might not be prepared to hear.

661
00:42:30,300 --> 00:42:35,000
We're not responsible for bringing about fruit, but when we listen obediently, we will be moved to action.

662
00:42:35,000 --> 00:42:40,480
We will respond, and the seed of the kingdom will be spread through us, which Corey will talk more about next week.

663
00:42:40,480 --> 00:42:42,940
So this is the parable of the sower.

664
00:42:42,940 --> 00:42:46,100
If you have ears to hear, please hear it, okay?

665
00:42:46,100 --> 00:42:53,440
I'm going to pray, and then Ryan will send us forth to pursue Christian community this week.

666
00:42:54,200 --> 00:43:00,840
Father God, I so thank you for this church, and I thank you for the durable parables that you've given us.

667
00:43:00,840 --> 00:43:09,680
I thank you for the meaning in them that will elicit action from us, that will make us more like you.

668
00:43:09,680 --> 00:43:21,220
And I pray that that would just grow in us this week, and that we would listen to your words and hear more from that parable than, you know, clearly than I said today.

669
00:43:23,900 --> 00:43:29,840
Let us be your hands and feet to our brothers and vehicles for growing the kingdom in this world.

670
00:43:29,840 --> 00:43:31,020
In Jesus' name, amen.
